Depends: passwd, ffmpeg
Suggests: postgresql | mariadb-server, nginx | caddy
Description: Self-hosted live-streaming studio
 StreamGo is a browser studio: invite guests, put cameras and screens on
 stage, and go live to RTMP and RTMPS destinations (YouTube, Twitch,
 Facebook, your own server), served by one static binary with the web app
 embedded.
 .
 Everything is installed in /opt/streamgo, with the LiveKit and MediaMTX
 servers the studio needs, and runs as the streamgo user under systemd
 (streamgo.service, streamgo-livekit.service, streamgo-mediamtx.service).
 The database is SQLite by default, or MariaDB or PostgreSQL. The program is
 encoded with the distribution's ffmpeg.
